.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-OLLAMA-INSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-ollama-install
.Nd install the Ollama runtime from the image, and the network only when asked
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -allow-network
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The one way kldload installs Ollama; first boot and the automatic
deployment both call it.
.Nm :
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
does nothing more when a working
.Pa /usr/local/bin/ollama
is already there;
.It
otherwise unpacks the runtime the image carries into a staging
directory, checks the binary runs, and only then moves it into
.Pa /usr/local ;
a copy that is there but broken is a failure, and nothing is installed;
.It
only when the image carries no runtime and
.Fl -allow-network
is given, downloads Ollama's own
.Pa install.sh
and runs it;
.It
makes the
.Ql ollama
user and
.Pa ollama.service
if they are missing, without enabling or starting it: its callers add
their drop-ins first.
.El
.Pp
Running it again changes nothing.
It needs root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -allow-network
When the image has no runtime, fetch Ollama's installer from
.Lk https://ollama.com/install.sh .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_OLLAMA_RUNTIME , Ev KLDLOAD_OLLAMA_PREFIX , Ev KLDLOAD_OLLAMA_UNIT_DIR
The runtime archive, the install prefix and the unit directory, for
tests.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/darksite/ollama/runtime/ollama-linux- Ns Ar arch Ns Pa .tar.zst
The runtime the image carries.
.It Pa /usr/local/bin/ollama , Pa /usr/local/lib/ollama/ , Pa /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service
What it installs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the runtime is installed and runs; 1 when it failed; 2 on a usage
error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
In a Fedora 44 container, which carries no runtime:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-ollama-install
kldload-ollama-install: FATAL: no Ollama runtime in the image (/root/darksite/ollama/runtime/ollama-linux-amd64.tar.zst) and --allow-network not given
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-ai-webui 8 ,
.Xr kldload-firstboot 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-13 an install meant to be offline piped
.Pa ollama.com/install.sh
into
.Xr sh 1 ,
which failed adding NVIDIA's repository; and first boot's own copy from
the image had no service to enable.
.Nm
replaced both.
